1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----<br/>
2 CONT '''For overview of Eide farm and Eide line, consult Kindem’s Vossaboki II, Eide, pages 26-35.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 26, 27 Eide.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ……….<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Eide. 28<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT See more about him at Finne in Volume I.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ....farmer in 1640 and '''Velom Nilsson, g. m. Agota, in 1645'''. Dordei then was the housekeeper and Kari the servant girl.  '''Johannes Seve owned 2 pund in Eide in 1652''', Viking Ygre ‘/1 laup in 1655, Viking Ygre and Gyri Rek
2 CONC ve each a pund in…<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Eide. 29 In the tax census of 1657 of the Finne Properties it states that it owned 5 laup in Eide.  '''Velom''' was the cotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Velom Nilsson'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1691 Klas Miltzow owned 2‘/2 laup 8 mark, Vangen’s parsonage 2 laup l pund 9 mark, the operators 8 mark and Sjur Hylle l spann. The cotters were '''Velom and his son Gusskalk''' who each had half the farm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parish minister Henrik Miltzow, in 1662, sued Velom Eide for rent''' and tredjetage of the deserted property Ho and presented a compensation letter from six men, the magistrate and the clerk, dated 1634. Then there was listed, 
2 CONC among other things, what each shareholder owned, rental and more. Miltzow further presented Reverend Buck’s land register, which showed that the land assessment was 2 laup and also 2 mmb. in Ho. Besides, Rannveig Olavsdr. Olde own
2 CONC ed 2 laup and 1 box of grain (sold to Isak Lunde), the Giske Properties ‘/1 laup, Endre Seve ‘/2 pund, Isak Lunde (purchased by Jon Mutuen) 1 pund and Arnbjrarn Gjerde 1 pund 1 mmb. and 1 box of grain. All this combined to be the 
2 CONC rent for Eide and Ho. Also presented was a 12-men ruling…<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 30 Eide.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Velom’s son Gusskalk was the cotter in 1691 on half of Eide until he died in 1699. He was married with Synneva Persdr., who died in 1746, 81 years old.'''They owned l pund in Hatlestad. Gusskalk was the postal farmer in the 169
2 CONC 0’s with a salary of 2 rd. 4 mark and got some reduction of his taxes. Velom, Gusskalk’s father, the postal farmer in the 1680’s, had his tax reduced by 2 spann smrar and 2 buckskin. About 1716 Nils Eide was the mail farmer with a
2 CONC  salary of2 rd. 4 mark and a uniform allowance of 5 mark 3 skill. a year. At the estate settlement after Gusskalk there was among other things: a silver bowl valued at 4 riksdalar, a silver belt at 4 rd., a gun at 2 rd. '''Gusskal
2 CONC k and Synneva had these six children : Velom f. 1692''', Guro f. 1685 (was a widow in 1746), Anna f. 1687, g. m. Arne, Brita f. 1690, g. m. Eiliv Flogo, Agota f. 1695, g. m. Mons Larsson Tveito, and Kari f. 1697, g. m. Olav Upphei
2 CONC m, Vestb.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Synneva was married again with Nils Larsson''', probably from Staup, f. 1680. They got the deed in 1700 and 1704 on 3 laup 1 pund 4 mark and operated the whole farm. At the estate settlement after Nils in 1737 the gross was 686
2 CONC  rd. '''Nils and Synneva had four children: Gusskalk f. 1707''' (bruk 2),<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[see note at end of this presentation regarding Nils Larsson Staup and Synneva Persdotter Fykse]'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Ragnhild g. m. Anders Mikkjelson Lid, Kv., Ingebjorg married to Molster with Mattis Bjarneson, and Kari, g. m. Knut Person Seim. From now it was two farms with the dividing line at Eide, bruk 1 and 2.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The individual bruk.''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruk I. Eide. The forenamed '''Velom Gusskalkson, who was bom in 1692, married in 1712 with Rannveig Bjarnesdr. Molster and died in 1746.''' He was relieved of from military service by being a postman at Eide. Parish minister Wein
2 CONC wich leased in 1712 to Velom, 2 laup 9 mark in Eide and ‘/1 pund in Kolle. Velom traded with his mother in 1738 for 1 laup 2 pund 4‘/2 mark in Eide and purchased of it in 1742 1 pund 14‘/2 mark, which at the estate settlement in 1
2 CONC 746 was valued at 125 rd. He also owned 1 pund in Hatlestad. '''Velom and Rannveig’s children were:''' Gusskalk f. 1710, Bjarne f. 1723 (came to Rote), Guri (g. m. 1. Nils Olavson Dolve, 2. m. Lars Bo), Brita (g. m. Corporal Per l
2 CONC varson Rekve), Anna f. 1726 (g. m. Anders Andersson Vestrheim at Store Rate),<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 31 Eide.<br/>
2 CONT '''Sigvor f. 1728 (g. m. Eiliv Johannesson Berge). Velom’s heirs sold it''' for the 2 pund 141/2 mark he had bought it, '''to Knut Gusskalkson.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 32 Eide.<br/>
2 CONT Bruk 2. Eide. …..Knut got from his father’s estate what he had owned in the farm and in 1751 bought from Velom Gusskalkson’s heirs 2 pund 14‘/2 mark.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 33 Eide…..'''Knut Gusskalkson Eide married the second time in 1842 with Brita Johannesdr. Hovda''' and he died 1885. With his ﬁrst wife Knut had the daughter Margreta f. 1832, and '''with his second wife three children : Brita d. 
2 CONC e. f. 1845, Brita d. y. f. 1848, married to Seim, Viki, with Nils Eirikson, Anna f. 1850, married to Seim with Olav Nilsson.'''<br/>
2 CONT The oldest daughter Margreta was married in 1860 with Ivar Ivarson Bo. They got the farm in 1864 for 900 spd. Margreta died in 1904 and Ivar in 1910. They had the son Ivar f. 1868. He and his half-brother Gusskalk Steffason, who w
2 CONC as the son of Margreta, got the purchase contract on the farm in 1905. Ivar Ivarson married with Elisabet Hansdr. Sakvitno and died in 1922. Gusskalk f. 1856 was married with lngebjorg Gusskalksdr. Uppheim and died in 1922. She go
2 CONC t, in 1923, the deed from the estate settlement from Ivar for his part in the farm for 3750 Crowns.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[Additional information on relationships not explicit in above account:'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Larsson Staup + Synneva Persdotter Fykse<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Gusskalk Nilsson Eide + Anna Knutsdatter Raustad<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Gusskalkson Eide + Anna Olavsdatter Liland<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Gusskalk Knutson Eide + Margreta Knutsdatter Finne<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Gusskalkson Eide + Brita Johannesdatter Hovde<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Brita Johannesdatter Hovde was the daughter of Johannes Kolbeinson Hovde and Brita Brynjulvsdatter Liland Hovde and sister of Kolbein Johannesson Hovde (1798-1876).]
2 CONT
2 CONT ……………
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
