1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Knut Torgeirson Kvåle leased the farm (Skutle) in 1837. He was born in 1800, and in 1836 married Elsa Johansdatter Vinjo, born in  1813. She was of the Blombergätti family. Knut co-founded Voss Sparebank and was a 
2 CONC member of the board for several years. Elsa died in 1861 and Knut in 1864. They had seven children: Guri born 1837, and in 1866 married Knut Knutson Helland, Johan Sechmann born 1839, Torgeir orn 1842, and married Eli Massdatter E
2 CONC ide, who owned a house at Eide in Granvin, Lars born 1843, married Margreta Larsdatter Apaltun (both to America), Sisselja Susanna born 1846, died unmarried in 1927, Maria born 1849, and in 1869 married Per Sjurson Vike, Bjarne bo
2 CONC rn 1851, died unmarried in 1886.
2 CONT
2 CONT The  [https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savings_banks_in_Norway Voss Sparebank] [https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voss_Veksel-_og_Landmandsbank Photograph today]
2 CONT
2 CONT The bank's books do not say anything about who made the admission to start the bank, but the son of one of those who were involved has told about it as follows: Arnoldus Koren in Seim, mayor of Voss 1842-49, wrote to the following
2 CONC  10 men and asked if they would like to join and form a bank and put together some money to start with. The 10 were: David L. Hustveit, Anders S. Leiddal, Nils J. Lid, Sjur P. Ringheim, Knut T. Kvarakvål, Anders V. Gjerme, Jens Ri
2 CONC venes, Isak Gjelle, Anders Tvilde and Knut T. Skutle. They met, agreed to deposit their 10 special dollars each in the bank and announced that they accepted deposits. 400 dollars soon came in. Then Koren said: “Yes, now I have don
2 CONC e well, I have accepted deposits, but no one has signed up to borrow.” Then there was a Lustring who bought a farm in Dukstad. He borrowed all the money from the bank. For a long time, the bank could not afford to buy itself a fir
2 CONC eproof cabinet to hide money, books and securities in. The cashier then took the money home, and Nils Lid carried the books home to Lid after each meeting.
2 CONT
2 CONT The books in the bank show that the first plan is dated 22 April 1842 and approved by royal resolution. 14 June 1843. The Founders, 24 men, were self-proclaimed supervisors and gave 10 dollars each, (one gave 20 and one 15 dollars
2 CONC .) This money, 255 dollars in total, was called "security deposit". The 24 were: Nils J. Lid, Jens Rivenes, Knut T. Skutle, Anders T. Røte, Anders Tvilde, David Hustveit, Torstein J. Vinjo, Torgeir A. Kvåle, Sjur P. Ringheim, Arnf
2 CONC inn E. Finne, Lars L Saude, Mass A. Finne, Viking O. Rykke, Olav A. Flatekvål,
2 CONT Anders V. Gjerme, Styrk A. Fjose, district doctor Hans Wille, coroner Jens Skagen, Herlaug Flatekvål, Anders Leiddal Knut L. Rokne, Nils A. Finne, Knut Øvsthus and Arnoldus Koren.
2 CONT
2 CONT A meeting was held on 15 November 1843, where most of the members were present. Then David Hustveit, Jens Rivenes and Nils J. Lid were elected as directors and A. Koren as treasurer. "Bank meetings" were initially only held every 
2 CONC second Sunday, later every Sunday and first in 1857 on working days. First they stayed in the courtroom (at plot 49), then in the house that stood where Voss Veksel- og Landmandsbank is now (at plot 72), later in a chamber in the 
2 CONC Heradshuset. The bank then remained open every Monday afternoon from 14-17. Later, the bank rented a house from Styrk Ullestad (tuft 66), in 1867 bought the old arrest room (at tuft 40) and moved there. In 1873, the house was exte
2 CONC nded and a height was added. The bank then remained in the second floor until 1909, when he bought the property on the corner of Lekvesgata and Vossagata (tuft 32-36) and moved there. Now the bank has built a new three-storey bric
2 CONC k house appropriate for the period and moved into it in the summer of 1932.
2 CONT
2 CONT As members left, they elected new men. A new plan was adopted in 1888. There were still 24 in the board of trustees, but half were to be chosen by the trustees, one-fourth by the district board and one-fourth by the board of trust
2 CONC ees. After a new revision of the plan in 1926, the depositors selected 20 men and the county board 4. The board of trustees selected the board of directors, auditors and inspectors and appointed a cashier and other employees in th
2 CONC e bank. Among those who have been on the board the longest can be mentioned: Nils J. Lid 41 years, Jens Rivenes 39 years, Johannes Finne 9 years, Knut T. Skutle 15 years, Odd Mølster 15 years, Josef N. Lid 43 years, Tormod Vinsand
2 CONC  36 year.
2 CONT The board is now (circa 1933): Klas J. Finne since 1888, chairman since 1922, Olav Bjørgum and Isak Gjelle since 1921. The treasurers have been: Arnoldus Koren 1843-50, Johannes Finne 1850-74, Ola Litsheim 1850-86, Odd Mølster 187
2 CONC 4- 1908, and then Lars Skutle. The auditors are now L. Hustveit and Knut Lydvo. Teacher Mass Haga is chairman of the board of trustees.
