1 NAME Anders Knutson /Fadness/
2 GIVN Anders Knutson
2 _MARNM Fadness
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 8 OCT 1823
2 PLAC Evanger, Voss, Hordaland, Norway
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 JUL 1910
2 ADDR
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anders Knudson Fadnes was baptized on Jan 4, 1824 in Evanger, Norway, the fourth child of Knud Gullickson Fadnes and Ingebjor Olsdatter Rongen. He married Ragnilde Hendriksdatter Fadnes in Norway and they emigrated
2 CONC  together in April 1848 on the ship "Augusta". In America, he spelled his name Andres.
2 CONT
2 CONT After settling in Keyeser, Columbia County, WI for 20 + years, the family moved to Mitchell County, IA in 1869. Andres lived there until he died and was returned to Spring Prairie Lutheran Church Cemetery for burial, according to 
2 CONC his wishes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Andres had seven siblings: Gulleik (Aug 1812) who immigrated in 1854, Ole or Olav (Feb, 1814) who immigrated in 1845, Anna (Sep 1820) who married Odd Knutsson Brunborg and immigrated to Spring Prairie, WI in 1848, and younger sibl
2 CONC ings: Nils (Jul 1826) who immigrated in 1848, Endre (1828) who immigrated in 1848, Haldor (1832 – 1832), and Torbjørg Knutsdatter (1834) who immigrated in 1848 and married Johannes Sjursson Berstad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders’ father, Knut Gulleiksson Fadnes married a second time in 1848 to Inger Brynjulvsdatter Skjerveggen (1813) and immigrated in 1848. He became farmer in Spring Prairie, WI and is buried there. They had three more children.
