1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----<br/>
2 CONT '''For overview of Berge farm 1730 and Berge line, consult Kindem’s Vossaboki II, Berge, pages 68, 69 as well as Bruk 5, page 72.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1730, Johannes Styrkson and Johannes Larsson are listed as owner and operators of Berge.  The latter was from Gjerde and he was a grandson of Johannes Sverkveson Seve, who was married with the first wife of Sheriff Mass Seve.  
2 CONC Johannes Larsson (1698-1778) was married to Steinvor Kolbeinsdatter (1701 -1752).  They had six children and they sold their share of Berge in 1748.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Styrkson Rue (1696-1783) was married secondly to Brita Kolbeinsdatter and they also had six children, one of whom was also a Kolbein (born 1736 who married Kari in 1765).  The fact that two Kolbein Johannesson Berges were
2 CONC  born within a few years of each other has been a source of considerable confusion among family historians.  However, the fact is that the Kolbein who married Kari is not in the Robert Hovde great-grandparent line.  He is a great 
2 CONC uncle.
2 CONT
2 CONT The one who is of note among the six children of Johannes and Brita is Eiliv.  Eiliv Johannesson Berge (1728-1802) in 1753 married Sigvor Velomsdatter Eide (1728-1801).  They are the GG04 for Robert Louis Hovde.  They had ten chil
2 CONC dren and their son, Velom Eilivson Berge (1759-1810) in 1798 married Kari Olavsdatter Tesdal (-1808).  Velom was convicted of striking and killing a fellow named Mattis Mousson Berge so Velom was sent to prison, five years hard la
2 CONC bor.  Velom and Kari are GG03 of Robert Hovde.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Bruk 5. Berge<br/>
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Velom noted above was the owner of Bruk 5.  He had only one child, his daughter Sigvor (1800).  The farm was leased to Styrk, Velom’s brother.  Styrk’s son, Eiliv Styrkson, born 1806 married Guro Nilsdatter Rote, they farmed for a
2 CONC  period and in 1857 sold the farm and went to America with their family.  One son, Knut Burgh (1838-1875), was a professor at Luther College and John a Lutheran pastor.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigvor Villumsdatter Berge in 1822 married Kolbein Johannesson Hovde and are the GG02 of Robert Louis Hovde and the parents of Brynjolf Kolbeinson Hovde, who in 1868 married Elisabeth Albertine Henriette Hovde.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruk 5 eventually ended up with Olav Johannessen Hovda and wife, Marta Vaete.
2 CONT ----
