3 CITY Eau Claire
3 STAE Wisconsin
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This was written by a person at the Nyre family re-union of 1983
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars and Kari moved from Dane County to homestead in beautiful Bennett Valley. It is located south of Mondovi and east of Gilmanton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT One of Lars and Kari's grandchildren remembers that Lars designed and made all the tools he needed to work the land and build the shelters for his large family and for the animals the he acquired.  He built a loom on which cloth a
2 CONC nd rugs were woven. He made a spinning wheel and after wool was sheared from the sheep and the wool was washed and dyed and carded, it was spun into yarn on the homemade spinning wheel and later woven into cloth for suits and dres
2 CONC ses. The yarn was knitted into sweaters, mittens, and stockings. Ann Nyre-Alberson inerited that loom and continued to use it for many years to weave numerous rugs for her children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars built a log cabin for their first home, but later built a ten room house over a basement where the vegetables, canned fruits and meats, which had  been smoked and roasted and canned for preservation were stored. This was befo
2 CONC re refrigeration.
2 CONT
2 CONT The original large home burned and today on that location is a modern house that is occupied by the Duane Gray family, a great-grandson of Lars and Kari.  Lars L Nyre  Birth 18 Dec 1831  Norway Death 1 Aug 1910 (aged 78)  Lookout,
2 CONC  Buffalo County, Wisconsin, USA Burial  Lookout Lutheran Church Cemetery  Mondovi, Buffalo County, Wisconsin Family Members Spouse
2 CONT
2 CONT Kari Knutsdatter Brunborg Nyre  1841–1910 (m. 1862)  Children
