1 NOTE Anders lived in Minneapolis, Arthur Markve sheets
2 CONT
2 CONT In Voss, Anders was a master builder for many years.  He emigrated with his son Knut to America in 1909.  Children Guri and Johannes left in 1911. Anders and Knut went on the ship "Oscar II", and landed in New York, traveled to Ar
2 CONC lington, South Dakota, and later to Glendive, Montana.  About 1922 Anders went to Fargo, North Dakota.  There he had a carpenter shop.  He was a member of the Norwegian Lutheran Church, Sons of Norway and Vosselaget.
1 NOTE Anders lived in Minneapolis, Arthur Markve sheets
2 CONT
2 CONT In Voss, Anders was a master builder for many years.  He emigrated with his son Knut to America in 1909.  Children Guri and Johannes left in 1911. Anders and Knut went on the ship "Oscar II", and landed in New York, traveled to Ar
2 CONC lington, South Dakota, and later to Glendive, Montana.  About 1922 Anders went to Fargo, North Dakota.  There he had a carpenter shop.  He was a member of the Norwegian Lutheran Church, Sons of Norway and Vosselaget.
