1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Michael Berge obit:6/13/1921 Cap. Times
2 CONT
2 CONT MICHAEL J. BERGE Michael J. Berge, living two miles south of Deerfield, passed away Saturday evening at 7 o'clock after an illness of about three weeks. Mr. Berge was 54 years old and leaves his wife and seven children: Mabel, Lyd
2 CONC ia, Joseph, Arthur, Agnes, John and Margaret.  The funeral will be held Wednesday at two o'clock at the home and at 2:30 at the Deerfield Lutheran Church, Rev. D. J. Borge officiating.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cap Times 6/15/1921:
2 CONT
2 CONT DEERFIELD - Michael Berge passed away at his home two miles south of town Saturday night after being confined to bed a month with cancer of the liver. He was born on the old homestead where he died, 54 years ago. He leaves besides
2 CONC  his wife, seven children, four girls and three boys, also two brothers, Bennie and Nickolai, and one sister, Ellen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held from the house at 2 o'clock Wednesday and from the Synod church at 2:30, conducted by Rev. D. D. Borge. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Cap Times 6/21/1921:
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mike Berge were held at the Synod church on Wednesday, conducted by Rev. D. D. Borge and the remains laid to rest beneath a wealth of flowers in the Synod cemetery west of town.  Pallbearers were Sam Aspinwell
2 CONC , Alfred Edwards, Lewis Dahle, Carl Mickelson, Andrew Brickson, and Hans Beckrum. 
2 CONT
2 CONT State Journal 6/13/1921:
2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY MICHAEL BERGE Michael J. Berge living two miles south of Deerfield died Saturday evening after an illness of about three weeks. Mr. Berge was 64 years of age. Besides his wife he is survived by seven children: Joseph, Art
2 CONC hur, Mabel, Lydia, Agnes, John, and Margaret. The funeral will be held Wednesday at 2:00 from the home and at 2:30 from the Deerfield Lutheran Church, the Rev. Mr. Borge officiating.
