1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Knute Nelson, born on the farm Kvilekval (Qvileqval),  Evanger, Voss, Norwegian-American politician (Republican), came to the U.S. in 1849 and grew up in Wisconsin. Participated in the American Civil War from 1861 
2 CONC to 1864, later legal education. Member of Wisconsin's legislature from 1868 to 1869 and of the Minnesota Senate from 1875 to 1878. Nelson was a member of Congress (House of Representatives) 1883-1892, 1892 was chosen as Minnesota'
2 CONC s governor, re-elected 1894. From 1895 until his death he was a member of the U.S. Senate.
2 CONT -
