1 NOTE 7 children Lived on a farm called Opheim, Stalheim in Voss.  Some of the family took the name Nelson and some called themselves Stalheim. One of his sons, Tormond went by first name of Thomas and his children used the last name of
2 CONC  Thompson.
2 CONT Immigrated in 1870. Only children who did not come were Brita, grandmother of Simon Hjornevik and Anna, grandmother of Helge Hjornevik. Nils lived in Beaver Creek, Wisconsin and died in Pigeon Falls, Wisconsin.See page 366 of Evan
2 CONC ker Boka II. He is thought to have been buried at the Tangen church but there is no marker indicating this. The old lutheran church has a family plot, Nelson, and some of children and spouses buried there. His wife, however, is bu
2 CONC ried at the new church.
2 CONT
2 CONT The churches split in 1878 and the new church built in 1888. Anna was first person buried at new church in 1889. The present (new) church built in 1949.
2 CONT
2 CONT Found reference to family in a Voss bygdabok which said he immigrated to America in 1867. This reference also said he lived at Beaver Creek, Wisconsin and died in Pigeon Falls, Wisconsin. when Nils immigrated with his wife, some o
2 CONC f his children came with him - Tom (Tormond), Nels and Martha and Olene. Already in the U.S. was daughter Ingrid. Two of the daughters, Brita and Anna, were married and remained in Norway.
