2 DATE 26 NOV 1926
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Guro Tone,
2 CONT widow of Thorbjorn (Thomas) K. Ton, Gilman, lowa, died last November 26.
2 CONT She was born at Voss June 15, 1842 a daughter of David Oddson Klove and his wife Inger neé Mon.
2 CONT She was from Voss' most prominent families. Her grandfather, Odd Davidson Klove was a member of the extraordinary Storting in 1814 and her father was a much involved man in public service at Voss.
2 CONT He was an elector several times and a deputy Storting representative one time. He was on the town council for many years. Her mother was from the Losna and Riber families. There were eight siblings in the family of whom five came 
2 CONC to America. These were: Brynjulv Klove, who died in the Civil War, Lars, who lived in Northwood, lowa, Ingeborg Vinje in Dunbar, IA, mother of Supreme Court Justice Vinje in Wisconsin, and Sigrid (Mrs. N. Selheim) Gilman, IA. At V
2 CONC oss remained the brothers Odd Klove, Johannes at Hylle, Birta Ovsthus and Arnguna Nyre.
2 CONT Guro married Thorbjorn Knutson Ton or Tvilde on July 6, 1862 and after three years they immigrated to America. On the 4" of July that same year they came to Decorah, IA traveling through Chicago, IL, and Prairie du Chien, WI.
2 CONT After a year near Decorah they took a homestead in Emmett County, IA and stayed there eight years, whereupon they got a farm in Marshall County, IA where they stayed until Torbjorn's death in 1922, when Guro moved to Gilman, IA.
2 CONT They had 13 children of whom 10 survive their parents. Among them are David and Elmer, lawyers in Chicago. See the rest in Vossingen No. 2- 4th year.
2 CONT Guro Tone is described as a good, kind woman with a strong personality. The burial took place at Stavanger Quaker Church's cemetery six miles from the town.
