1 NAME Sigvor Villumsdatter /Berge/
2 GIVN Sigvor Villumsdatter
2 SURN Berge
2 NICK SIGVOR WILLUMSDR
2 NICK Sigvor Villiamsdatter
2 NICK Sigvor Velomsdatter
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1800
2 PLAC Berge, Voss, Hordaland, Norway
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 DEC 1892
2 PLAC Hovde
2 ADDR
3 CITY Voss
3 STAE Hordaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''For overview of Berge farm 1730 and Berge line, consult Kindem's Vossaboki II, Berge, pages 68, 69 as well as Bruk 5, page 72.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 68 Berge
2 CONT
2 CONT ……..<br/>
2 CONT '''In 1730, Johannes Styrkson and Johannes Larsson are listed as owner and operators. The latter was from Gjerde and exchanged in 1729 with Erling Rognaldson for 2 laup in Berge. Johannes was a grandson (son’s son) of Johannes Sve
2 CONC rkveson Seve, who was married with the ﬁrst wife of Sheriff Mass Seve. Johannes Larsson who died in 1778, 80 years gl., was g. m. Steinvor Kolbeinsdr. dead 1752, 51 years gl. and had six children. He sold the farm in 1748''' to Ar
2 CONC nved Jonson Skjerve. Continued bruk 1. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johannes Styrkson Rue was g. l. m. Brita Styrksdr., 2. m. Brita Kolbeinsdr., who died in 1783, 87 years gl.''' In 1727, he bought 2 laup in Berge. At his estate settlement in 1743 are listed '''six children: Styrk, Eiliv, Kolbe
2 CONC in, Hallstein, Synneva and Brita.''' Styrk was g. 1746 m. widow Barbra Jakobsdr. Lisseim. '''Kolbein f. 1736 married in 1765 m. Kari Knutsdr. Lunde.''' Hallstein
2 CONT
2 CONT 69 Berge.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT f. 1730 was g. 1766 m. Kari Andersdr. Lisseim. Brita married in 1750 m. Per Olavson Lisseim. '''Eiliv was f. 1728, died in 1802, and was g. 1753 m. Sigvor Velomsdr. Eide. They had 10 children.''' Eiliv, in 1757, got the deed from 
2 CONC his siblings for 2 pund 8 mark, in 1773, the deed from his mother for 1 laup, bought from Hallstein Lisseim, his brother, in 1773, 6 mark in Ovre-Berge, and bought the redemption rights for 2 laup in Berge in 1760 for 33 rd. 66 sk
2 CONC ill. Gabriel Marselis had bought the property in 1657. In 1783, Eiliv leased to his oldest son, Johannes, 1 laup and in 1788 to his son Velom 1 laup. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johannes f. 1755, died in 1810, and was g. 1783 m. ek. Marta Ivarsdr. Bo. They didn’t have children. He leased the farm to Velom, his brother.''' He also leased l laup again in 1798 to his brother-in-law, Kolbein Person Gavle. 
2 CONC Continued at bruk 4. In addition, Velom bought in 1798 from his father 12 mark in Ovre- Berge. '''Velom f. 1759, died in 1810, was g. 1798 m. Kari Olavsdr. Tesdal, dead 1808. In 1804, he was before the court for having struck Matt
2 CONC is Mousson Berge with a grain pole, so he died about a month later. Velom was sentenced''' to “work in irons” for 5 years at Bergenhus fortress. He also was to pay a compensation judgment and court costs. Continued at bruk 5.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ……….
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The individual bruks.''  
2 CONT
2 CONT 72  Berge.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bruk 5.'''  Berge.   Above is told that '''Velom Eilivson was owner of this bruk.''' He had only his '''daughter Sigvor f. 1800 and leased the farm in 1811 to Styrk, his brother,''' for 1000 rd. '''His son, Eiliv Styrkson got t
2 CONC he farm in 1825. He went to America and sold the farm in 1857 to Ingebrikt Olavson for 1050 spd.  Eiliv was f. 1806 and g. 1823 n1. Guri Nilsdr. Rate. One of their sons, Knut, f 1838, who used the name Bergh, was a professor at Lu
2 CONC ther College, Decorah. He died in Granvin 1875. lngebrikt leased the farm again in 1860 to Olav Brynjulvson, who was g. m. Kristi, daughter of Eiliv Styrkson, mentioned above. They sold it again in 1865 to Olav Johannessen Hovda f
2 CONC or 550 spd. His widow, Malta Brynjulvsdr., was g. m. Svein Andersson Kvale, who got the deed on the farm in 1874.'''     
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
