2 CONT Mickelson, Mrs. Agnes L.DEERFIELD - Mrs. Agnes L. Mickelson, age 98, died on Sunday, April 19, 1987, at the WIllows Nursing Home in Sun Prairie. The former Agnes Thompson was born on December 15, 1888, in Deerfield Township. on Ja
2 CONC nuary 11, 1908, she married Carl Mickelson, and together they farmed in the Deerfield area. She was a member of St. Paul's Liberty Lutheran Church, the Sarah Circle, and the Deerfield American Legion Auxiliary. She is survived by 
2 CONC a son, jeromy "Totsy" of Deerfield; a daughter, Doris (Roger) Engelstad of Cambridge; and a daughter-in-law, Betty Mickelson of Deerfield; four grandchildren and five great-grandchildren. She was preceded in death by her husband i
2 CONC n 1939; a son, Edward in 1980; a son and daughter in infancy; and by two brothers and three sisters. Funeral services will be held on Wednesday, April 22, at 11:00 a.m. at ST. PAUL'S LIBERTY LUTHERAN CHURCH, with the Reverned Lowe
2 CONC ll Mays officiating. Burial will be in the church cemetery. Friends may call at the funeral home in Deerfield from 5:00 until 8:00 p.m. on Tuesday. 
