1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Mrs. Lund ServicesCAMBRIDGE - Funeral services for Mrs. Andrew Lund, 78, who died Tuesday at her home here, will be held Thursday at 2 p.m. in St. Paul's Liberty Prairie Lutheran church.  The Rev. Enoch J. Tetlie will officiate an
2 CONC d burial will be in the church cemetery.  The former Annie E. Thompson, Mrs. Lund was born at Crystal Lake, Ill. She had lived in the Cambridge area for 55 years, the past 33 years having resided in the village.  She was married o
2 CONC n Sept. 21, 1897 in London, Wis. She was a member of the Ladies Aid society of St. Paul's Liberty Prairie Lutheran church.  Survivors include her husband; three daughters, Mrs. Oscar Gjerald and Mrs. Otto Sorum, Deerfield, and Mrs
2 CONC . Albert Storlie, Cambridge; three sons, Harold and Eugene, Cambridge, and Alfred, Deerfield; a sister, Mrs. Agnes Mickelson, Deerfield; a brother, Arthur Thompson, Tomah; seven grandchildren and seven great-grandchildren. Friends
2 CONC  may call at the NItardy funeral home here after noon today. 
