1 OCCU Lensman (Norway Sheriff).
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Story of Sjur's children and their emigration to the U.S.:
2 CONT https://www.gilderhus.org/the-red-booklet/emigrating-to-america
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Excerpts from Minnie Holtan's Memories==
2 CONT Giljarhus was our grandparents’ name in Norway; the letter H is silent. This name was later changed to Gilderhus here in the United States. Here is a brief sketch of our great-grandparents and their family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sjur A. Giljarhus was born in Voss, Norway in 1762, and died in 1848. He married Marta Larsdatter Veka in 1796. She died in 1842, 67 years old. Six children were born to Sjur and Martin Giljarhus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders born in 1798
2 CONT Anna     ”       ” 1800
2 CONT Lars    ”        ” 1802
2 CONT Gunnvor   ”    ” 1805
2 CONT Nils          ”     ” 1808
2 CONT Ola          ”     ” 1814
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunnvor married Andrew Lee, and is Julia Lee Reque’s mother. Lars, my grandfather, married Randvei Seim in Norway in 1844. I do not know who the other children of Sjur and Marta Giljarhus married, but I know Nils Gilderhus as he w
2 CONC as later named, was Lauritz Gilderhus’ father, and grandfather of Nordeen, Reuben, and Donald Gilderhus.
2 CONT
2 CONT A “thank you” to Julia Lee Reque, who has furnished us with names and dates of our great-grandparents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sjur Giljarhus was a “lensman” in Norway, similar to a sheriff here in the United States. Four children were born to Lars and Randvei Gllderhus:
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha born in Norway, 1845
2 CONT Kristens born in Cambridge, Wisconin, Sept. 26, 1854
2 CONT Severt born in Dodge County, Minn., 1861
2 CONT Anna born in Dodge County, Minn., 1864
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Other Information==
2 CONT Birth:  1758, Norway  Death:  1848 Hordaland County, Norway 
2 CONT
2 CONT On a gently sloping hillside overlooking a beautiful lake in Voss, Norway, lies a farm by the name of Giljarhus. This name actually means "a house near a ravine or gulch". Down through the years the spelling became changed to Gild
2 CONC erhus. This was due to the Danish influence. Norway was under the rule of Denmark for several hundred years.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the early and middle 1800's, this farm was owned by Sjur Giljarhus and his wife, Marta Larsdatter Vika. They had six children -- their names in order of age were: Andres, Anna, Lars, Gunvor, Nils, and Ole.
2 CONT
2 CONT They all immigrated to the USA.
2 CONT *  Nels  arrived July 6, 1839, as did his sister  Anna  and her husband Knute Brekke. and  Ole K Gilderhus  who is possiby a 1st cousin.
2 CONT *  Ole S  in summer of 1840
2 CONT *  Gunvor came 1841 with her husband Andres Lee.
2 CONT *  Andres came in 1843
2 CONT *  Lars  came 1950. 
