1 NOTE Baard var fra Voss
1 NOTE There was boat traffic from Bergen to Vesterålen for many years, perhaps centuries, because the Hanseatic league bought the "torsk" from the fishermen.  Because of this, it was natural for Bård to make the trip to north Norway wit
2 CONC h the established water route.  The boats commonly used were called "jekt", about 60 to 70 feet long.  Many immigrated to the area for employment in the fishing industry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bård moved from Voss because the large family limited possibilities for employment.  When he came to Vesterålen, he worked and then took over the farm and married.  In addition to fishing, he also farmed (2 or 3 cows) and harveste
2 CONC d wood and peat moss.  His farm was about 30 dekar in size.  One dekar is 10 meters square.  The old house was about 5 X 8 meters in size and stood where Dennis Baardsen has now built a hytte.
1 NOTE There was boat traffic from Bergen to Vesterålen for many years, perhaps centuries, because the Hanseatic league bought the "torsk" from the fishermen.  Because of this, it was natural for Bård to make the trip to north Norway wit
2 CONC h the established water route.  The boats commonly used were called "jekt", about 60 to 70 feet long.  Many immigrated to the area for employment in the fishing industry.
2 CONT
