1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Ex-Christiana Farmer, Is Dead DEERFIELD - Andrew T. Tillung, 87, Deerfield, a long time Town of Christiana farmer until his retirement in 1955, died today in a Stoughton nursing home. He was born in the Town of Christiana in 1880,
2 CONC  the son of the late Mr. and Mrs. Ole Tillung. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On March 5, 1906, he was married to Amelia Kingland of the Town of Christiana. She died in 1967.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Tillung was a member of the West Koshkonong Lutheran Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are a son, Olin, Deerfield; a brother, Bennie, West Covina, Calif.; a sister, Mrs. Albert Anderson, Rice Lake; one grandson, and three great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call at the Holzhuter Funeral Home, Deerfield, from 2 p.m. Sunday until noon Monday, when the body will be taken tot he West Koshkonong Lutheran Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral rites will be held in the church at 2 p.m. Monday, with the Rev. Gerald Anderson officiating. Burial will be in the church cemetery. 
