1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Lewis Tillung Rites CAMBRIDGE-Funeral services for Lewis Tillung, 68, who died Wednesday in a Chicago hospital after a brief illness, will be held at 2 p. m. Saturday in the West Koshkonong Lutheran church, where he was a member.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Rev. Henry Thompson, pastor, will officiate, and burial will be in the church cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Tillung, who was a farmer,was born in the town of Christiana.  On Mar. 31, 1923, he was married to the former Cora Johnson.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife; a daughter, Mrs. Theodore Swenson, Cambridge; a sister, Mrs. Albert Anderson, Rice Lake; Four brothers, Iver, and Martin, both of Rice Lake: Benny, Chicago, and Olin, in California, and three grandchild
2 CONC ren.
