1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Olin Tillung Olin B. Tillung, 63, 1104 Gilson St., died unexpectedly Thursday at his home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Tillung, a resident of Madison for the past seven years, was bornin Christiana township.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served with the Merchang Marine during most of his life and was a Wordl War I Army veteran.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are two daughters, Mrs. Tony Segro, 1104 Gilson St., and Mrs. wilbur Bardin, Walnut Creek, Calif.; three grandshildren; four brothers, Andrew, Deerfield; Iver and Martin, Rice Lake; and Benjamin, West Covina, Calif.; and
2 CONC  a sister, Mrs. Albert Anderson, Rice Lake.
2 CONT
2 CONT The body was taken to the Frautschi funeral home here, and friends may call there from 11 a.m. Sunday until time of services.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral rites will be held Monday at 10:30 a.m. in the funeral home, with Rev. J. Donald Rice of St. Mark's Lutheran Church here officiating.  Burial will be in the Cambridge Methodist cemetery.
